Hello community,

I have already seen some discussions about oomkills on AB during last coupl=
e weeks.
When I have updated poky 458c39ac1f81932bb92afaef098ea618c54bb737 to 903710=
ab5c4ea3c13dd1abf5accdefd27d3a5bdc I observe the memory overuse also on my =
machine (gitlab runner in VirtualBox x84-64, Debian 12, 16 cores, 16 thread=
s, 32GB RAM, 50% zram).
So it's "only" 242 commits to inspect what could have caused this.

What I have from the events is a screenshot of ps output from the moment wh=
en the gitlab-runner VM died.
It shows that the testsuite is running cmake with "-j" without number.
This instructs it to spawn as many threads as needed (e.g. thousands for bi=
g projects like clang).
There wasn't any eye-catching change in the 242 commit diff, the most attra=
ctive was cmake upgrade.
But it can also be that Yocto always did this and cmake 3.x reacted differe=
ntly than cmake 4.x.

Does anyone have quick insight which part of code is involved here?

Peter

